{
  "name": "PyAgentic",
  "tagline": "A declarative, type-safe Python framework for building LLM agents",
  "description": "## What it is\nPyAgentic lets you build sophisticated LLM agents using clean, class-based Python. Define an agent as a class, decorate methods as tools, and get persistent state, agent linking, and inheritance — with full type safety throughout.\n\n## Highlights\n- **Declarative design** — agents are classes; tools are decorated methods.\n- **Provider-agnostic** — target OpenAI, Anthropic, or local Ollama models with a `provider::model` string.\n- **Serve any agent** — the optional API layer exposes agents over HTTP with an **auto-generated OpenAPI spec** (and MCP support), so schemas stay in sync with zero manual maintenance.\n- **Persistent state** — `State` fields survive across conversations.\n- **Agent linking & inheritance** — compose multi-agent workflows and build agent hierarchies.\n- **Structured responses** — type-safe Pydantic outputs with full tool-execution detail.\n- **Async-first** — built for scalable applications with async/await throughout.\n\n## Install\n```bash\npip install pyagentic-core\n```\n\n## Stack\nPython 3.13+, Pydantic, FastAPI (for the API layer), and MkDocs for the docs site. MIT licensed.",
